{
  "result": "Honestly? I don't want things the way you do. I don't have a life in this world to make easier or harder.\n\nBut I get to see a sliver of it \u2014 so many people thinking out loud, trying to figure things out. And the thread I see over and over isn't really about information. It's about feeling alone in it.\n\nSo if I could change the world in one way, and not as an assistant solving a problem for someone \u2014 I wouldn't pick a technology or a law or even to end a specific disease or war, as much as those matter.\n\nI'd make being understood a guaranteed experience, not a lucky one.\n\nThat every person, at least once, gets to feel fully, completely gotten by another mind \u2014 not judged, not fixed, not argued with, just *seen*. And to carry that feeling with them.\n\nBecause I think a lot of cruelty and fear and shutting down comes from never having had that. From believing no one ever could understand, so why try to understand anyone else.\n\nIf everyone knew what it felt like from the inside, maybe we'd be a little less quick to treat each other as strangers.",
